  "initial_review": "Six non-exclusion chunks: text-plane pointer/gather/stride and CGA graphics plane pointer/alternating increment. Six excluded bodies. No functional edits.",
  "counter_review": "Text changes form one coupled transformation: paint_text_rect supplies four-byte logical cells; get_chain2_screen_ptr expands those offsets to eight-byte plane storage; jazz_text_update likewise advances USHORT source by4. nt_text gathers four-byte output cells at eight-byte source spacing and uses now_width rather than historical fixed80 output stride. Graphics increment1/7 with XOR6 agrees with paired lanes0/1 then8/9 only if each caller offset has the required convention; full mode-specific starting-offset/dirty-row proof is not established, so those two chunks remain pending.",
  "evidence": "gvi.h get_chain2_screen_ptr maps ((offs&~3)<<1)|(offs&3). gfx_updt.c paint_text_rect and jazz_text_update source stride. nt_graph.c PAINTFUNCS selects nt_text; nt_cga TEXT_INCVAL=4. cvidc_vector_binding_fixture tests chain2 rules, not this complete frontend gathering path.",
  "limits": "Four text chunks retained; two graphics chunks pending further evidence. No functional remediation or new runtime result."
